ests on fundamentals and polls.", "New or vacant seat with no expert ratings; fundamentals only.", "No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings."]}, "overview": "Maryland remains one of the most Democratic-leaning states in presidential elections, and the outlook for this open race reflects that advantage. The incumbent Republican president is term-limited, so neither side carries incumbency into the contest. No public polls of the state, expert ratings, or market pricing are available, leaving the forecast to rest on the state's partisan fundamentals.\n\nHeadlines from Maryland center on the governor's race, redistricting fights, and 2028 primary speculation rather than the presidential contest itself, offering little signal about the general-election margin. With information this thin, uncertainty stays wide, but the structural lean points clearly toward the Democratic ticket, with an outside chance that a strong national environment shifts the race closer.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9506, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9102, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9258, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9194, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9194, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9136, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9144, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9103, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9184, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.9155, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9262, "margin": 16.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.91, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.9155, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.9104, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.9151, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.9188, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.9069, "margin": 15.0}, {"dat